  "notes": "Commons' recent photos are all from the right; the left is taken to be the same with the fin bands mirrored and the titles in the same places. Drawn from the A321neo (longer than the generic body): the wave's crest and trough sit relative to the wing. The scheme has been essentially unchanged since launch (2006), refreshed only in small details; ATR 72s carry the same. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on VT-IRZ (right side, side-on): the fuselage title runs x 0.138 to 0.28 as drawn (lowercase 0.73 of the I); the fin title runs about 0.8 of the chord where it starts; the engine's 'goIndiGo.in' from 0.17 to 0.70 of the nacelle. The wave and both light-blue stripes are curves along their whole length: smooth.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. IndiGo's scheme since its first A320 (2006)."
